  "$comment": "The top of the road, and where Frost finally gets to be what the country is: thirty-two of every hundred against the climb's twenty-four. That is a deliberate step up and it is the last one -- the Frost Hall is on the other side of the col and a player who has come this far has met the type on a route before meeting it in a Hall, which is the order every type in this game is introduced in.\n\nStone still carries the rest of it, for the reason the climb's note gives: it is the one type neutral against all three starters both ways, and a table this high has no room to be unfair as well as high. Menhir is on it at six -- the only fully evolved Stone line in the wild anywhere in Caelora -- and meeting one should be an event rather than a tax.\n\nTHE WATER TABLE IS THE HOLE IN THE ICE, and it is the strangest table in the game on purpose. Deeplum is a Tide/Umbral that the Vellum places in a lake, and this is the lake. Four fifths of it is under two feet of ice and dark all winter. Levels are 32-37 against a team-raiser arriving at about 38.",
